{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-\u00e6on/1273616-trinity-continuum-\u00e6on-clarifications","id":1273616,"title":"Trinity Continuum \u00c6on Clarifications","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","The Trinity Continuum","Trinity Continuum: \u00c6on"],"posts":[{"date":"2018-12-09T12:53:53-08:00","id":1273616,"title":"Trinity Continuum \u00c6on Clarifications","content":"In the \u00c6on book:<br /> <br /> p. 264: In the Vitakinetic power &quot;Direction&quot;, it says:<br /> &quot;The psion can also either temporarily increase or decrease the speed vitakinesis of biological processes, like breathing or healing by successes spent&quot;<br /> Q: How do I measure this? doubling/halfing duration per success? Or is there a table where I can increase/decrease by steps?<br /> <br /> <br /> General question:<br /> <br /> In the core book, p. 65: Can the &quot;Artifact&quot; edge only be taken by Talent characters? What if my psion wants his own spaceship or so? Is there some kind of edge similar to the old 1e background &quot;Device&quot; which can take care of this? Would this edge cost be similar to that of the old background?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3122-shuragil","name":"shuragil","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"41"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-09T13:52:03-08:00","id":1273626,"title":"","content":"p. 53: &quot;Most power has devolved to local regions in a grand experiment of autonomy.&quot;<br /> p. 54: &quot;Unlike the voluntary social experiment of Germany [...]&quot;<br /> Q: What is this experiment? It's not described anywhere in the book.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3122-shuragil","name":"shuragil","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"41"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-14T09:04:05-08:00","id":1274369,"title":"","content":"Page 216: The first sentence of the System text for Compartmentalize states that a certain effect occurs whenever the power is active. Does this mean that as long as the biokinetic has bioware that he is attuned to at the lower cost due to this power's effects, that secondary effect is also always occurring?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23768-graywulfe","name":"graywulfe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23768_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"16"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-23T17:02:41-08:00","id":1276332,"title":"","content":"p.333 TC: Aeon (Under Sub-Aberrant) &quot;...observers who dissect dead Aberrants find that most don\u2019t possess the signature Mazarin-Rashoud structures...&quot;<br /> <br /> Q: What are these? Not defined in Trinity Continuum: Aeon or the Core rules. Internet searching tells me this is like the genetic component that allows an Aberrant to use Quantum??? Regardless its not defined anywhere in this iteration of the game.<br /> <br /> Additionally a section describing the basics of Quantum and Noetics and how they relate (also how they relate to Flux) would be appreciated. Been trying to piece this together, especially after reading the Secrets Chapter of TC: Aeon but I really don't have a grasp of how they are related (opposed?) and it seems pretty core to understanding what's going on in this game. <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24925-wraith","name":"Wraith","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-23T19:35:59-08:00","id":1276352,"title":"","content":"TC: Aeon p.193 talks about Illness and Disease being modeled through conditions and talks about setting a Severity and Virulence for the disease. It also references the TC: Core Rules.<br /> <br /> TC: Core Rules p.106-108 talks about Other Forms of Damage and appears to be what the TC: Aeon book above is referencing. However this section never talks about Severity or Virulence. In fact in never talks about setting the Severity (bruised, injured, maimed.)<br /> <br /> Q: How are diseases and illness supposed to be handled. Like TC: Core rules or how TC: Aeon suggests? Should these be the same?<br /> <br /> Note: TC: Aeon called for a Survival+Stamina (Skill+Attribute) role to resist a disease while TC: Core Rules calls for a Stamina+Resolve (two Attributes) roll.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24925,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24925-wraith","user":"Wraith","date":". 12-23-2018, 10:41 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24925-wraith","name":"Wraith","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-23T20:18:14-08:00","id":1276364,"title":"","content":"TC: Aeon p.203 both Scrub and Trace call for Enigmas rolls, not Enigmas+Attribute.<br /> <br /> Q: Should the roll only consist of Enigmas or should there be an attribute attached to it?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24925-wraith","name":"Wraith","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-24T04:21:39-08:00","id":1276425,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wraith</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-\u00e6on/1273616-trinity-continuum-\u00e6on-clarifications?p=1276352#post1276352\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">TC: Aeon p.193 talks about Illness and Disease being modeled through conditions and talks about setting a Severity and Virulence for the disease. It also references the TC: Core Rules.<br /> <br /> TC: Core Rules p.106-108 talks about Other Forms of Damage and appears to be what the TC: Aeon book above is referencing.</div> </div> </div> </div>It\u2019s not. TC: AEon is referencing pp. 104 (Injury Conditions) to 106 (Status Conditions). TC: Core \u2018Other Forms of Damage\u2019 doesn\u2019t reference illness and disease, it talks about fire, radiation, and poison. <br /> <br /> Illnesses are treated as per TC: AEon. The specifics of how illnesses work and progress aren\u2019t very cinematic action drama so weren\u2019t included there. Since one psi Aptitude specifically works against illness and disease, we included rules for how they work in AEon.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-24T04:27:04-08:00","id":1276427,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>graywulfe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-\u00e6on/1273616-trinity-continuum-\u00e6on-clarifications?p=1274369#post1274369\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Page 216: The first sentence of the System text for Compartmentalize states that a certain effect occurs whenever the power is active. Does this mean that as long as the biokinetic has bioware that he is attuned to at the lower cost due to this power's effects, that secondary effect is also always occurring?</div> </div> </div> </div>No. Incorporating formatted bioware is a separate effect of this power that doesn\u2019t mean the rest of the power is active.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-25T10:50:29-08:00","id":1276666,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>shuragil</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-\u00e6on/1273616-trinity-continuum-\u00e6on-clarifications?p=1273626#post1273626\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">p. 53: &quot;Most power has devolved to local regions in a grand experiment of autonomy.&quot;<br /> p. 54: &quot;Unlike the voluntary social experiment of Germany [...]&quot;<br /> Q: What is this experiment? It's not described anywhere in the book.</div> </div> </div> </div>Intricate details are likely too much to get into in this book, given its existing page count.<br /> best source of information currently available would be the 1E book, Shattered Europe.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24507-baladain","name":"Baladain","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"68"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-28T21:01:04-08:00","id":1277301,"title":"","content":"p.243 TC: Aeon under the Drain power... the final sentences of this power hint at the Doyen (or at least let a player reading the section know about them.) Is this intentional. Other information on them is relegated to the secrets chapter at the end of the book?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24925-wraith","name":"Wraith","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-04T11:04:26-08:00","id":1278641,"title":"","content":"Do we know if Defense is supposed to be so different from Scion? In Scion it states that you only roll Defense the first time you are attacked, and that is your defense for the rest of the round. The attack resolution summary where that is stated in Trinity doesn't have that same stipulation.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Raksha are my fae-vorite.<br /> <br /> Reincarnation of magnificentmomo.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1542-morosemorgan","name":"MoroseMorgan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1542_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"778"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-04T15:55:35-08:00","id":1278717,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MoroseMorgan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-\u00e6on/1273616-trinity-continuum-\u00e6on-clarifications?p=1278641#post1278641\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Do we know if Defense is supposed to be so different from Scion? In Scion it states that you only roll Defense the first time you are attacked, and that is your defense for the rest of the round. The attack resolution summary where that is stated in Trinity doesn't have that same stipulation.</div> </div> </div> </div>I\u2019ve added it to the Core errata for clarification.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-05T00:45:01-08:00","id":1278781,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>shuragil</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-\u00e6on/1273616-trinity-continuum-\u00e6on-clarifications#post1273616\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In the \u00c6on book:<br /> <br /> p. 264: In the Vitakinetic power &amp;quot;Direction&amp;quot;, it says:<br /> &amp;quot;The psion can also either temporarily increase or decrease the speed vitakinesis of biological processes, like breathing or healing by successes spent&amp;quot;<br /> Q: How do I measure this? doubling/halfing duration per success? Or is there a table where I can increase/decrease by steps?</div> </div> </div> </div>I\u2019ve added this to the errata thread as it clearly needs clarification.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-05T10:48:05-08:00","id":1278839,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MoroseMorgan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-\u00e6on/1273616-trinity-continuum-\u00e6on-clarifications?p=1278641#post1278641\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Do we know if Defense is supposed to be so different from Scion? In Scion it states that you only roll Defense the first time you are attacked, and that is your defense for the rest of the round. The attack resolution summary where that is stated in Trinity doesn't have that same stipulation.</div> </div> </div> </div>Where in Scion Origin does it say you only roll defense for the first attack? Scion seems equally ambiguous to me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24935-werlynn","name":"werlynn","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"192"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-05T12:13:19-08:00","id":1278843,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>werlynn</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-\u00e6on/1273616-trinity-continuum-\u00e6on-clarifications?p=1278839#post1278839\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Where in Scion Origin does it say you only roll defense for the first attack? Scion seems equally ambiguous to me.</div> </div> </div> </div>p.115.<br /> <br /> 1 Declare your target (or targets) and choose your dice pool. The target(s) declare the Defense action they wish to take, and roll for a Defensive action if it\u2019s their first time in the turn being attacked.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-05T14:08:25-08:00","id":1278860,"title":"","content":"Huh. They should have put it in the full text of defense.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24935,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24935-werlynn","user":"werlynn","date":". 01-05-2019, 05:17 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24935-werlynn","name":"werlynn","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"192"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-07T06:32:37-08:00","id":1279183,"title":"","content":"Originally posted by <b>shuragil</b> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1273616-trinity-continuum-\u00e6on-clarifications#post1273616\">View Post</a><br /> In the \u00c6on book:<br /> <br /> p. 264: In the Vitakinetic power &amp;quot;Direction&amp;quot;, it says:<br /> &quot;The psion can also either temporarily increase or decrease the speed vitakinesis of biological processes, like breathing or healing by successes spent&quot;<br /> Q: How do I measure this? doubling/halfing duration per success? Or is there a table where I can increase/decrease by steps?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bunyip</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-\u00e6on/1273616-trinity-continuum-\u00e6on-clarifications?p=1278781#post1278781\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I\u2019ve added this to the errata thread as it clearly needs clarification.</div> </div> </div> </div>Maybe use the same mechanics as the biokinetic power Metabolic Control (p. 213)?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3122-shuragil","name":"shuragil","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"41"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-07T08:26:43-08:00","id":1279219,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bunyip</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-\u00e6on/1273616-trinity-continuum-\u00e6on-clarifications?p=1278717#post1278717\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I\u2019ve added it to the Core errata for clarification.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks! Sometimes it is difficult to figure out what is intentionally different or not, and I didn't want to add too much noise to the errata thread.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Raksha are my fae-vorite.<br /> <br /> Reincarnation of magnificentmomo.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1542-morosemorgan","name":"MoroseMorgan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1542_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"778"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-07T12:16:26-08:00","id":1279278,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bunyip</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-\u00e6on/1273616-trinity-continuum-\u00e6on-clarifications?p=1276425#post1276425\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It\u2019s not. TC: AEon is referencing pp. 104 (Injury Conditions) to 106 (Status Conditions). TC: Core \u2018Other Forms of Damage\u2019 doesn\u2019t reference illness and disease, it talks about fire, radiation, and poison.<br /> <br /> Illnesses are treated as per TC: AEon. The specifics of how illnesses work and progress aren\u2019t very cinematic action drama so weren\u2019t included there. Since one psi Aptitude specifically works against illness and disease, we included rules for how they work in AEon.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks for the clarification. Suggestion... It seems illness and disease are something that could appear in any era, Should those rules maybe be in Trinity Core. Otherwise you'd have to reprint them in each era's source book? I'm sure their will be nova healers? Or so I'd imagine.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24925-wraith","name":"Wraith","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-10T08:07:18-08:00","id":1279904,"title":"","content":"What do the armor damage type tags do? Not all powers that grant soft armor include such tags so what do they protect against? There is a \u201ccomplete\u201d tag for all damage types so if the intent was \u201call types\u201d why don\u2019t those powers include the complete tag?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24935-werlynn","name":"werlynn","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"192"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-10T08:12:33-08:00","id":1279905,"title":"","content":"Is there any sort of way to resist the \u201cdefensive\u201d armor tag? It seems very harsh. You could have 6 levels of soft armor making you close to bulletproof and stabproof, but a spiky suit of armor will murder you in a fist fight.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24935-werlynn","name":"werlynn","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"192"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-10T08:20:25-08:00","id":1279907,"title":"","content":"If you activate multiple levels of the same mode in a single action how does the enhancement bonus apply? Say I have augendis 5 and I want to activate levels 1 through 4 in one action to boost myself up. Normally I get an enhancement on each power equal to the number of additional mode dots I have. Do I add 4 (he highest) or 1 (the lowest) to the whole roll? Do I add 10 to the whole roll? Do I just add the individual enhancements to their respective powers?<br /> <br /> My confusion comes from general confusion over how to apply enhancement bonuses to mixed actions since those rules seemed to say you include all the bonuses and just apply them however you want, so a gun shooting enhancement could be applied toward balancing on a speeding train in a mixed action. That seeems weird.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24935-werlynn","name":"werlynn","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"192"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-10T11:30:00-08:00","id":1279932,"title":"","content":"I believe the language on enhancements in the multiple actions rules limits the enhancements to being applied where appropriate... I could be misremembering.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23768-graywulfe","name":"graywulfe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23768_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"16"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-12T05:03:43-08:00","id":1280297,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wraith</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-\u00e6on/1273616-trinity-continuum-\u00e6on-clarifications?p=1276332#post1276332\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">p.333 TC: Aeon (Under Sub-Aberrant) &quot;...observers who dissect dead Aberrants find that most don\u2019t possess the signature Mazarin-Rashoud structures...&quot;<br /> <br /> Q: What are these? Not defined in Trinity Continuum: Aeon or the Core rules. Internet searching tells me this is like the genetic component that allows an Aberrant to use Quantum??? Regardless its not defined anywhere in this iteration of the game.<br /> <br /> Additionally a section describing the basics of Quantum and Noetics and how they relate (also how they relate to Flux) would be appreciated. Been trying to piece this together, especially after reading the Secrets Chapter of TC: Aeon but I really don't have a grasp of how they are related (opposed?) and it seems pretty core to understanding what's going on in this game.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>The Mazarin-Rashoud node, or MR Node, is a gland in the brain that gives a Nova/Abberant their powers. I'm sure it will be fully fleshed out, pun intended, in the Trinity Continuum: Aberrant book. There's really no need for it in the Aeon book. <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=485\" data-tempid=\"temp_485_1538393298974_786\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1277-karpomatic","name":"karpomatic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1277_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"143"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-17T21:42:49-08:00","id":1281449,"title":"","content":"Flash says you make an attack with enhancement equal to your mode dots. Is this attack the same psi roll you used to activate the power or separate? You already get a potential enhancement equal to how many dots your rating exceeds the power you\u2019re using. Then there is favored mode\u2019s 2 enhancement. It\u2019s a hard edge to pass up.<br /> <br /> Would a PK with thermokinesis 4 and that mode favored throw a enhancement 8 blast?<br /> <br /> I\u2019m not saying it\u2019s not balanced. You don\u2019t get to throw too many of those. I\u2019m just checking that I have the math right.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24935-werlynn","name":"werlynn","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"192"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-21T04:44:36-08:00","id":1281927,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>werlynn</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-\u00e6on/1273616-trinity-continuum-\u00e6on-clarifications?p=1281449#post1281449\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Flash says you make an attack with enhancement equal to your mode dots. Is this attack the same psi roll you used to activate the power or separate? You already get a potential enhancement equal to how many dots your rating exceeds the power you\u2019re using. Then there is favored mode\u2019s 2 enhancement. It\u2019s a hard edge to pass up.<br /> <br /> Would a PK with thermokinesis 4 and that mode favored throw a enhancement 8 blast?<br /> <br /> I\u2019m not saying it\u2019s not balanced. You don\u2019t get to throw too many of those. I\u2019m just checking that I have the math right.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hey, sorry, missed this question when it was posted. <br /> <br /> Short answer, yes the attack and psi activation are the same roll, and yes, you get all that Enhancement. It\u2019ll fry any humans you\u2019re up against, but the Legions will need it when facing off against Aberrants.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-21T14:20:45-08:00","id":1282011,"title":"","content":"If you use something like an Interface Augmentation Device does your mode and psi count as 1 higher for purposes of where you are on the charts on 208 and 209? Could you potentially count as the next level of radius or duration?<br /> <br /> Example: I have psi 3 and augendis 3. Augendis powers last my mode dots times my duration. Do they last 4 minutes or 4 hours when I use an interface augmentation device?<br /> <br /> Do I count as having mode +1 for the purpose of determining the base enhancement of activating powers that I have higher mode dots for?<br /> <br /> Example: Same character activates stoicism (augendis 2). Without the IAD I would get a +1 enhancement because I have augendis at 3 dots. Would I count as 4 dots and get a +2 enhancement with the IAD?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24935,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24935-werlynn","user":"werlynn","date":". 01-21-2019, 05:27 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24935-werlynn","name":"werlynn","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"192"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-22T12:47:25-08:00","id":1282179,"title":"","content":"With the computer enhancement edge it requires you to buy SIX additional dots in edges. Why not just make it that expensive? Those separate edges wouldn\u2019t go away if your computer goes away (like if your EK used the biocomp version) because you\u2019re buying them separately. It feels like the computer enhancement edge should also enhance those other edges or make them cheaper while you have the computer, so then if you lose the computer you have to buy up the difference in cost for the other edges.<br /> <br /> You\u2019d only even be able to buy all those if you worked them into your other paths because 6 of your starting edge dots are locked to path edges. Maybe buying computer enhancement should grant those edges immediately with an XP debt of their cost.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24935-werlynn","name":"werlynn","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"192"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-23T09:15:32-08:00","id":1282296,"title":"","content":"My guess in Vehicle Combat:<br /> Vehicles have 3 Condition box, I would say Scratch (no complications), Minor Damage (-1), and Several Damage (-2), as the vehicle don\u2019t have a bad effect from the pain, just from missing and broken parts.<br /> Scratch are just that, no penalities, but still some damage. Armour tag gives extra scratch box.<br /> Minor damage are things that make the vehicle operate a little bad, like a broken whindshield, but still don\u2019t restrict it in general. Massive tag add extra Minor damage boxes.<br /> Several damage are damage to the motor or other important part, like tires and flaps, but the vehicle can still operate on limited ways.<br /> As characters, after it, there is the taken out box, that makes the vehicle stop working, like broken wheel, or propelers. It may be able to safely (or almost) land if it\u2019s flying, but the pilot would suffer a -4 complication that, if not payed will destroy the entire vehicle beyond repair.<br /> <br /> All the actions the pilot takes for manoeuver the vehicle are Pilot checks, substituting all the Athlectics checks needed for sprint, jump and crossing barriers.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-23T09:34:41-08:00","id":1282298,"title":"","content":"About the Super science section:<br /> On Adventure there are 2 kinds of super science, Advanced (done by daredevils) and Innovative Super science (by stalwarts and mesmerists). Advance super science is just improvements on regular tech, on Storypath terms, adding tags and enhancements, so no flying backpacks or freezing rays. Innovative Super science add knacks the the device, as whel as improvements, so a device with tags and enhancements, but also powers (modes from Aeon).<br /> <br /> On TC: Core there are 3 kinds, advanced, Inspired and powered. I would say that Advanced alow you to pick equipments form Aeon to use as devices (but no biotech), using the rank as 1 + cost (or more if more advanced or less for less advanced). Inspired add enhancements, tags, edges and gifts (the stunt described in the end of section), I would say using the rank as cost from standard equipments and tags, but also allowing to add tags that are not in Core list (aeon). Finally powered super science use the 1 + mode as rank for the effect and rank 1 if it is a bonus on mode rank or psi from the user or effects similar to basic powers from the aptitudes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-25T11:37:06-08:00","id":1282687,"title":"","content":"For Iatrosis 5 Adjust Template what is the cap for attributes? The various Augendis modes can take you to 7, which is even better the similar level biokinesis powers. I thought Vitakinesis was limited to things within the human range, so would that mean Adjust Template can go to 7?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24935-werlynn","name":"werlynn","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"192"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-25T11:57:49-08:00","id":1282693,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>werlynn</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-\u00e6on/1273616-trinity-continuum-\u00e6on-clarifications?p=1282687#post1282687\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For Iatrosis 5 Adjust Template what is the cap for attributes? The various Augendis modes can take you to 7, which is even better the similar level biokinesis powers. I thought Vitakinesis was limited to things within the human range, so would that mean Adjust Template can go to 7?</div> </div> </div> </div>I would say the maximum available to that person, as it is the human maximum as described, for most people would be 5, but 6 if the person is tier 3 or have superior trait edge for the attribute being adjusted.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-25T12:14:06-08:00","id":1282695,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mateus Luz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-\u00e6on/1273616-trinity-continuum-\u00e6on-clarifications?p=1282693#post1282693\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I would say the maximum available to that person, as it is the human maximum as described, for most people would be 5, but 6 if the person is tier 3 or have superior trait edge for the attribute being adjusted.</div> </div> </div> </div>Then I wonder why Augendis can go to 7 without some sort of limit of being at proxy-level to exceed 5. Even a biokinetic needs like 5 dots in their mode to break the 5 barrier.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24935-werlynn","name":"werlynn","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"192"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-25T12:25:18-08:00","id":1282697,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>werlynn</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-\u00e6on/1273616-trinity-continuum-\u00e6on-clarifications?p=1282695#post1282695